Recreate this page | add the logo attached and the altitude chart when the HTML code references Altitude Operating System Loop image | feel free to change the interface to make it better looking, ensuring brand colors are used | <!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Altitude - Stop Winging It. Start Operating.</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'Helvetica', Arial, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.6;
            color: #1a1a1a;
            background: #ffffff;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 0 20px;
        }

        /* Hero Section */
        .hero {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2d5c7f 0%, #3d9eb5 100%);
            color: white;
            padding: 80px 0 60px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .hero h1 {
            font-size: 3.5rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            margin-bottom: 24px;
            line-height: 1.15;
            letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        }

        .hero .subheadline {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            font-weight: 400;
            margin-bottom: 32px;
            line-height: 1.5;
            max-width: 900px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
            opacity: 0.95;
        }

        .qualification {
            display: inline-block;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
            padding: 16px 32px;
            border-radius: 50px;
            font-size: 1rem;
            font-weight: 500;
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
        }

        /* Pain Section */
        .pain-section {
            padding: 80px 0;
            background: #f8f9fa;
        }

        .pain-section h2 {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            color: #2d5c7f;
        }

        .pain-intro {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            color: #555;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto 60px;
        }

        .pain-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
            gap: 30px;
            margin-top: 40px;
        }

        .pain-card {
            background: white;
            padding: 40px 30px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
            border-left: 4px solid #3d9eb5;
        }

        .pain-card h3 {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            color: #2d5c7f;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .pain-card p {
            color: #555;
            line-height: 1.7;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
        }

        .pain-card .cost {
            margin-top: 20px;
            padding-top: 20px;
            border-top: 2px solid #f0f0f0;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #d9534f;
            font-size: 1.1rem;
        }

        /* Opportunity Cost Section */
        .opportunity-cost {
            padding: 80px 0;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2d5c7f 0%, #1a3a4f 100%);
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .opportunity-cost h2 {
            font-size: 2.8rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            line-height: 1.2;
        }

        .opportunity-cost .big-stat {
            font-size: 4rem;
            font-weight: 900;
            color: #50a684;
            margin: 40px 0 20px;
            line-height: 1;
        }

        .opportunity-cost p {
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto 30px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .opportunity-list {
            max-width: 700px;
            margin: 50px auto;
            text-align: left;
        }

        .opportunity-list li {
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            padding-left: 40px;
            position: relative;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .opportunity-list li:before {
            content: "→";
            position: absolute;
            left: 0;
            color: #50a684;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }

        /* System Section */
        .system-section {
            padding: 80px 0;
            background: white;
        }

        .system-section h2 {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            color: #2d5c7f;
        }

        .system-intro {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            color: #555;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto 60px;
        }

        .system-diagram {
            max-width: 1000px;
            margin: 60px auto;
        }

        .system-diagram img {
            width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
        }

        /* Layers Section */
        .layers-section {
            padding: 80px 0;
            background: #f8f9fa;
        }

        .layer {
            background: white;
            padding: 50px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
            border-left: 6px solid #3d9eb5;
        }

        .layer h3 {
            font-size: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
            color: #2d5c7f;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .layer .layer-question {
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #666;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .layer p {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            color: #555;
            line-height: 1.8;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        .layer ul {
            margin-top: 20px;
            padding-left: 20px;
        }

        .layer li {
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            line-height: 1.7;
            color: #555;
        }

        .layer.blue { border-left-color: #2d5c7f; }
        .layer.green { border-left-color: #50a684; }
        .layer.teal { border-left-color: #3d9eb5; }

        /* Burnout Section */
        .burnout-section {
            padding: 80px 0;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a3a4f 0%, #2d5c7f 100%);
            color: white;
        }

        .burnout-section h2 {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        .burnout-quote {
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            font-size: 1.5rem;
            font-style: italic;
            text-align: center;
            line-height: 1.7;
            padding: 40px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
            border-radius: 12px;
            border-left: 4px solid #50a684;
        }

        .burnout-stats {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
            gap: 30px;
            margin-top: 60px;
        }

        .burnout-stat {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px;
        }

        .burnout-stat .number {
            font-size: 3.5rem;
            font-weight: 900;
            color: #50a684;
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .burnout-stat .label {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            opacity: 0.9;
        }

        /* CTA Section */
        .cta-section {
            padding: 100px 0;
            background: white;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .cta-section h2 {
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            color: #2d5c7f;
        }

        .cta-section p {
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            color: #555;
            max-width: 700px;
            margin: 0 auto 50px;
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        .cta-button {
            display: inline-block;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #50a684 0%, #3d9eb5 100%);
            color: white;
            padding: 20px 50px;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 50px;
            transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(61, 158, 181, 0.3);
        }

        .cta-button:hover {
            transform: translateY(-2px);
            box-shadow: 0 15px 40px rgba(61, 158, 181, 0.4);
        }

        /* Footer */
        footer {
            background: #1a1a1a;
            color: white;
            padding: 40px 0;
            text-align: center;
        }

        footer p {
            opacity: 0.7;
        }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .hero h1 {
                font-size: 2.5rem;
            }

            .hero .subheadline {
                font-size: 1.2rem;
            }

            .pain-section h2,
            .system-section h2,
            .burnout-section h2 {
                font-size: 2rem;
            }

            .opportunity-cost h2 {
                font-size: 2.2rem;
            }

            .opportunity-cost .big-stat {
                font-size: 3rem;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero">
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Your Team Is Exhausted.<br>Another Quarter Won't Fix It.</h1>
            <p class="subheadline">
                Altitude installs a bias-resistant executive operating system so decisions, priorities, and narratives stay grounded in truth — even as the company scales.
            </p>
            <div class="qualification">
                For founder-led and PE-backed companies ($10M–$75M) that already feel the cognitive cost of scale
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pain Section -->
    <section class="pain-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>You've Crossed the Threshold</h2>
            <p class="pain-intro">
                Your instincts got you here. But now every decision requires three meetings, five Slack threads, and someone still drops the ball. You're not slow — you're running an operating system designed for 15 people with 50.
            </p>

            <div class="pain-grid">
                <div class="pain-card">
                    <h3>Strategy Keeps Drifting</h3>
                    <p>Priorities shift every quarter because there's no shared truth about what's actually working. Your leadership team argues over interpretation instead of execution.</p>
                    <div class="cost">Cost: 2-3 months per year lost to realignment</div>
                </div>

                <div class="pain-card">
                    <h3>Meetings Multiply, Clarity Doesn't</h3>
                    <p>You've added check-ins, stand-ups, and reviews. Yet somehow no one knows who's deciding what, or when something is actually done.</p>
                    <div class="cost">Cost: 30-40% of leadership time wasted</div>
                </div>

                <div class="pain-card">
                    <h3>Your Best People Are Breaking</h3>
                    <p>Top performers are working weekends just to keep up. Not because of the work — because the system has no rhythm. Everything feels urgent. Nothing feels clear.</p>
                    <div class="cost">Cost: Turnover of people you can't afford to lose</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Opportunity Cost Section -->
    <section class="opportunity-cost">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>What Another Quarter of "We'll Figure It Out" Actually Costs You</h2>

            <div class="big-stat">$750K–$2.3M</div>
            <p>That's the hidden drag of operating without a system. Not from bad strategy. From execution friction that compounds daily.</p>

            <ul class="opportunity-list">
                <li><strong>Strategic drift</strong> means you're 6-9 months behind where you could be if everyone pulled in the same direction</li>
                <li><strong>Decision latency</strong> costs you 2-3 major opportunities per year that competitors with faster systems capture</li>
                <li><strong>Team burnout</strong> means replacing a VP costs $300K+ and sets you back another quarter</li>
                <li><strong>Investor confidence</strong> erodes when your board sees the same issues recurring because insights don't translate to change</li>
            </ul>

            <p style="margin-top: 50px; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700;">
                Every cycle you delay is a cycle your team runs harder but moves slower.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- System Overview -->
    <section class="system-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>The Altitude Executive Operating System</h2>
            <p class="system-intro">
                Not another dashboard. Not another process layer. A complete operating architecture that connects strategy to reality and closes the loop automatically.
            </p>

            <div class="system-diagram">
                <img src="https://i.imgur.com/altitude-system-loop.png" alt="Altitude Operating System Loop" style="width: 100%; max-width: 1000px; display: block; margin: 0 auto;">
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Four Layers -->
    <section class="layers-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="layer blue">
                <h3>Layer 1: Strategic Direction</h3>
                <p class="layer-question">Where are we going, and what won't we do?</p>
                <p>This isn't your mission statement or OKRs. This is your <strong>True North</strong> — the strategic intent and guardrails that define what you're actually optimizing for, including what you'll deliberately ignore.</p>
                <p><strong>What you get:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Strategic initiatives mapped to measurable milestones</li>
                    <li>Clear constraints that prevent scope creep</li>
                    <li>A shared language for what "on strategy" actually means</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="layer green">
                <h3>Layer 2: Priorities & Bets</h3>
                <p class="layer-question">What are we betting on right now?</p>
                <p>Most companies have 40 priorities. You need 3-5 active strategic bets with clear owners and binary health signals. This layer forces focus design, not wishful thinking.</p>
                <p><strong>What you get:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Finite set of active initiatives (not a wishlist)</li>
                    <li>Clear ownership and accountability</li>
                    <li>High-level health tracking (On Track / Watch / At Risk)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="layer teal">
                <h3>Layer 3: Execution Rhythm & Signals</h3>
                <p class="layer-question">How do we know what's actually happening?</p>
                <p>This layer has two lenses: <strong>Health</strong> (Is the system holding together?) and <strong>Visibility</strong> (Are we operating as designed?). One is for triage. The other is for evolution.</p>
                <p><strong>What you get:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Cadence integrity monitoring (meetings, decisions, actions)</li>
                    <li>Exception-based escalation (early warnings before things break)</li>
                    <li>Pattern analysis (time allocation, drift detection, decision distribution)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="layer blue">
                <h3>Layer 4: Decisions & Consequences</h3>
                <p class="layer-question">Who decides — and what actually changes?</p>
                <p>Decisions without follow-through are just expensive conversations. This layer ensures every decision has an owner, linked actions, and completion evidence.</p>
                <p><strong>What you get:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Decision log with clear ownership</li>
                    <li>Automatic linkage from decision → action → outcome</li>
                    <li>Accountability for what actually changed (not just what was said)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="layer green" style="border-left-color: #2d5c7f;">
                <h3>The Executive Narrative: Closing the Loop</h3>
                <p class="layer-question" style="font-style: normal; font-weight: 600;">Governed sensemaking, not reporting</p>
                <p>This isn't a status update. It's how the CEO synthesizes all four layers into a coherent story of where the company is, where it's going, and what needs to change. The narrative turns reality into direction.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Burnout Section -->
    <section class="burnout-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>What Happens When You Install Altitude</h2>

            <div class="burnout-quote">
                "We thought we needed better people. Turns out we just needed a system that didn't burn out the ones we had."
            </div>

            <div class="burnout-stats">
                <div class="burnout-stat">
                    <span class="number">60%</span>
                    <span class="label">Reduction in leadership meeting time</span>
                </div>
                <div class="burnout-stat">
                    <span class="number">3x</span>
                    <span class="label">Faster strategic decisions</span>
                </div>
                <div class="burnout-stat">
                    <span class="number">Zero</span>
                    <span class="label">"Wait, who owns this?" moments</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Final CTA -->
    <section class="cta-section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Stop Waiting for the Right Quarter</h2>
            <p>
                Your team doesn't need another planning session. They need an operating system that makes clarity automatic, decisions traceable, and burnout preventable.
            </p>
            <a href="#" class="cta-button">See Altitude in Action</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
        <div class="container">
            <p>&copy; 2025 Altitude Operating System. Built for leaders who've outgrown winging it.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>

